 "briefing": "# Zepto Briefing: Changes from 16 October to 15 November 2026\n\n## Summary\n\nNo verifiable changes at Zepto were identified for 16 October to 15 November 2026. Every search attempt failed because the search tool hit its rate limit, so no news, launches, hires, or deals could be confirmed. This is not evidence that nothing happened. The window remains unchecked, and this briefing should not be read as confirming that the company was quiet.\n\n## Status by Dimension\n\n### News\nNo items were verified. Company news, regulatory matters, financial updates, and leadership statements for the window are unconfirmed.\n\n### Product Launches\nNo items were verified. Feature launches, new categories, private-label or fintech offerings, and pilots for the window are unconfirmed.\n\n### Executive and Key Hires\nNo items were verified. Changes to the CEO, CFO, CTO, COO, or board for the window are unconfirmed.\n\n### Deals and Partnerships\nNo items were verified. Funding rounds, valuation changes, acquisitions, commercial agreements, and IPO-related filings for the window are unconfirmed.\n\n## Recommended Actions Before 17 November\n\n- **Check the official newsroom and blog directly** for items dated 16 October to 15 November 2026. Zepto's public site is the most direct primary source, and it should be reviewed by hand because the search tool could not retrieve it.\n- **Review Indian business press with date filters**, including Economic Times, Mint, Moneycontrol, Inc42, Entrackr, Reuters, and Bloomberg, for coverage of any funding, leadership, or partnership announcements in the window.\n- **Check regulatory filings** on SEBI and the Registrar of Companies (MCA) for any IPO-related or corporate filings in the window.\n- **Re-run the search once the rate limit clears**, using the company name with narrow date-restricted terms for each category.\n\nEach item found through these steps should be logged with its date and URL before it is added to the briefing.\n\n## Three Open Questions for the Meeting\n\n1. Which announcements, launches, or leadership changes has Zepto made since mid-October 2026 that we should reflect in our planning, and where are they published?\n2. What is Zepto's current position on capital, funding, or any IPO preparation, and what is the expected timeline for the next milestone?\n3. Which partnerships or commercial agreements are being prioritised for the next quarter, and how would Zepto like to engage with us on them?\n\n## Sources\n\nNo citable sources were retrieved for the 16 October to 15 November 2026 window. No facts in this briefing are sourced, and none should be attributed to a source until it has been verified directly.",
